22nq|n|Chance; lot; destiny. ; A kind or species; any number or collection of individual persons or things characterized by the same or like qualities; a class or order; as, a sort of men; a sort of horses; a sort of trees; a sort of poems. ; Manner; form of being or acting. ; Condition above the vulgar; rank. ; A chance group; a company of persons who happen to be together; a troop; also, an assemblage of animals. ; A pair; a set; a suit. ; Letters, figures, points, marks, spaces, or quadrats, belonging to a case, separately considered.	a:aba,65,26;102q,53,3;1t15,23,22;1d3w,9,2;1xvf,5,100~1xvf,5,100;aba,65,26;1t15,23,22;102q,53,3;1d3w,9,2	n:15cj,62,4;9ci,36,4;wog,25,7;1d3w,23,5;1zg6,1,3~wog,25,7;1d3w,23,5;15cj,62,4;9ci,36,4;1zg6,1,3	N:2ect,28,9;1gvu,8,4;1j46,5,22~1j46,5,22;2ect,28,9;1gvu,8,4
