22rp|n|The person, body, or state in which independent and supreme authority is vested; especially, in a monarchy, a king, queen, or emperor. ; A gold coin of Great Britain, on which an effigy of the head of the reigning king or queen is stamped, valued at one pound sterling, or about $4.86. ; Any butterfly of the tribe Nymphalidi, or genus Basilarchia, as the ursula and the viceroy.	N:243a,54,2~243a,54,2
